WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.244 --> 00:00:01.998
- Wow, my stomach's gonna hate me later,

00:00:01.998 --> 00:00:04.200
but I don't care.

00:00:04.200 --> 00:00:06.316
I do what I want, OK?

00:00:06.316 --> 00:00:08.899
(upbeat music)

00:00:10.386 --> 00:00:11.772
- Hi, guys, my name is Matt.

00:00:11.772 --> 00:00:13.662
I am a Tasty Junior producer here

00:00:13.662 --> 00:00:15.099
in Los Angeles, California,

00:00:15.099 --> 00:00:17.461
and today I'm going to
be comparing the homemade

00:00:17.461 --> 00:00:20.272
and store-bought versions
of one of my favorite foods,

00:00:20.272 --> 00:00:21.433
macaroni and cheese.

00:00:21.433 --> 00:00:23.176
So I'm just gonna go prep my station,

00:00:23.176 --> 00:00:24.605
and then we can get down to business.

00:00:24.605 --> 00:00:27.261
(jazz music)

00:00:27.261 --> 00:00:29.005
Box mac and cheese is arguably

00:00:29.005 --> 00:00:30.345
one of the easiest things to make.

00:00:30.345 --> 00:00:31.178
Start to finish,

00:00:31.178 --> 00:00:32.744
it takes no more than 15 minutes.

00:00:32.744 --> 00:00:33.577
On the plus side,

00:00:33.577 --> 00:00:34.885
you only need two extra ingredients,

00:00:34.885 --> 00:00:35.827
milk and butter.

00:00:35.827 --> 00:00:36.886
On the down side,

00:00:36.886 --> 00:00:39.197
I honestly can't tell you
what kind of cheese this is.

00:00:39.197 --> 00:00:41.722
The box says it's original flavored.

00:00:41.722 --> 00:00:43.214
I have no idea what that means.

00:00:43.214 --> 00:00:45.366
I tried Googling it and found nothing,

00:00:45.366 --> 00:00:46.765
but it's cheap, it's easy,

00:00:46.765 --> 00:00:47.717
it's delicious,

00:00:47.717 --> 00:00:49.384
it's mac and cheese.

00:00:51.760 --> 00:00:53.309
- Ah.

00:00:53.309 --> 00:00:54.715
Actually haven't had it in a while.

00:00:54.715 --> 00:00:56.548
Just as good as I remembered.

00:00:56.548 --> 00:00:58.525
- It's better when you eat it like this,

00:00:58.525 --> 00:00:59.684
when you put it on the fork,

00:00:59.684 --> 00:01:00.530
and ah.

00:01:00.530 --> 00:01:02.133
- It tastes like I thought it would,

00:01:02.133 --> 00:01:03.383
which is to say

00:01:04.440 --> 00:01:05.574
like not much.

00:01:05.574 --> 00:01:07.442
- It's nostalgic, it brings you back.

00:01:07.442 --> 00:01:09.181
It's honestly pretty good.

00:01:09.181 --> 00:01:11.484
(jazz music)

00:01:11.484 --> 00:01:13.563
- [Matt] This one-pot recipe
was developed by Matthew,

00:01:13.563 --> 00:01:15.542
another one of our
producers here at Tasty.

00:01:15.542 --> 00:01:16.458
Like the box mac and cheese,

00:01:16.458 --> 00:01:17.654
it's super straight-forward,

00:01:17.654 --> 00:01:20.571
and you can make it all in one pot.

00:01:22.209 --> 00:01:23.393
Because you cook it in milk,

00:01:23.393 --> 00:01:24.900
you don't need to strain the macaroni,

00:01:24.900 --> 00:01:27.150
making everything creamier.

00:01:28.188 --> 00:01:29.863
By using real cheese, you
get that gooey texture,

00:01:29.863 --> 00:01:31.068
and authentic flavor.

00:01:31.068 --> 00:01:31.901
If you don't wanna use cheddar,

00:01:31.901 --> 00:01:33.943
go ahead and substitute
it with an equal amount

00:01:33.943 --> 00:01:35.450
of whatever cheese you'd like.

00:01:35.450 --> 00:01:37.867
(jazz music)

00:01:39.806 --> 00:01:40.639
And that's it.

00:01:40.639 --> 00:01:44.806
You had a homemade version
of boxed mac and cheese.

00:01:46.566 --> 00:01:48.353
- Definitely tastes like cheese.

00:01:48.353 --> 00:01:49.645
And like the other one,

00:01:49.645 --> 00:01:51.219
this is kind of like milk and noodle.

00:01:51.219 --> 00:01:53.870
- Definitely has a creamier

00:01:53.870 --> 00:01:54.942
consistency.

00:01:54.942 --> 00:01:56.202
- It's actually nice tasting,

00:01:56.202 --> 00:01:58.879
it's side-by-side Kraft,
you can really tell

00:01:58.879 --> 00:02:01.787
that the cheddar like
elevates the cheesy flavor,

00:02:01.787 --> 00:02:05.349
the real cheddar. (laughs)

00:02:05.349 --> 00:02:06.906
- [Matt] For this last mac and cheese,

00:02:06.906 --> 00:02:08.941
I wanted to do a real show-stopper,

00:02:08.941 --> 00:02:10.531
so we're going with a six cheese.

00:02:10.531 --> 00:02:12.074
To ensure things would be rich and creamy,

00:02:12.074 --> 00:02:13.270
I still it with a Bechamel,

00:02:13.270 --> 00:02:15.294
which is just a thick, milky white sauce

00:02:15.294 --> 00:02:16.932
that you see in a lot of classic recipes.

00:02:16.932 --> 00:02:18.407
It'll get a little clumpy at first,

00:02:18.407 --> 00:02:19.665
that is fine.

00:02:19.665 --> 00:02:23.832
It'll get smoother and creamier
as you keep adding more.

00:02:25.043 --> 00:02:26.557
Feel free to play around with what kind

00:02:26.557 --> 00:02:28.272
and how many spices you'd like.

00:02:28.272 --> 00:02:31.339
I went for smokey with
just a hint of spiciness.

00:02:31.339 --> 00:02:33.922
(upbeat music)

00:02:42.573 --> 00:02:43.797
I chose to use six cheeses

00:02:43.797 --> 00:02:46.374
for a blend of Sharps,
smokey and cream flavors.

00:02:46.374 --> 00:02:47.988
You don't need to add six cheeses,

00:02:47.988 --> 00:02:49.089
but why not?

00:02:49.089 --> 00:02:51.162
You get a more complex mix of flavors.

00:02:51.162 --> 00:02:54.495
Just make sure you use three cups total.

00:02:55.714 --> 00:02:58.152
Be aware, a lot of these cheeses
did not come pre-shredded,

00:02:58.152 --> 00:02:59.600
so I had to do it by hand,

00:02:59.600 --> 00:03:01.973
which was a lot more work.

00:03:01.973 --> 00:03:04.556
(upbeat music)

00:03:17.793 --> 00:03:19.601
To make this recipe really decadent,

00:03:19.601 --> 00:03:21.613
add a nice topping of
cheese and bread crumbs,

00:03:21.613 --> 00:03:22.664
and broil that.

00:03:22.664 --> 00:03:25.186
It'll give another layer
of texture and flavor

00:03:25.186 --> 00:03:28.853
that you don't get in
the first two recipes.

00:03:30.830 --> 00:03:32.897
While it takes twice the amount of time,

00:03:32.897 --> 00:03:34.953
more ingredients (laughs)
and much more effort,

00:03:34.953 --> 00:03:39.120
this mac and cheese will
really bring the house down.

00:03:41.644 --> 00:03:43.302
- Oh, wow.

00:03:43.302 --> 00:03:45.004
This is amazing.

00:03:45.004 --> 00:03:48.209
- There's definitely like
a lot more complexity.

00:03:48.209 --> 00:03:49.676
- Oh and there's a kick.

00:03:49.676 --> 00:03:50.598
- It's super cheesy,

00:03:50.598 --> 00:03:52.757
it's got like this little

00:03:52.757 --> 00:03:54.593
browned bread crumby bits,

00:03:54.593 --> 00:03:57.388
it's like a little salty in the best way.

00:03:57.388 --> 00:04:00.474
(stammers) this is amazing.

00:04:00.474 --> 00:04:03.057
(upbeat music)

00:04:04.344 --> 00:04:06.633
- My favorite, definitely

00:04:06.633 --> 00:04:08.678
is the fancy mac and cheese.
(bell dings)

00:04:08.678 --> 00:04:10.485
- I am (laughs) going to have to go

00:04:10.485 --> 00:04:12.957
with Kraft Mac and Cheese.
(bell dings)

00:04:12.957 --> 00:04:14.430
- I mean, without a doubt,

00:04:14.430 --> 00:04:15.959
the fancy, gourmet
(bell dings)

00:04:15.959 --> 00:04:17.191
mac and cheese is my pick.

00:04:17.191 --> 00:04:18.024
- I'm gonna have to go

00:04:18.024 --> 00:04:18.975
with the final one.
(bell dings)

00:04:18.975 --> 00:04:19.808
- I think

00:04:19.808 --> 00:04:22.009
I'm gonna got to go with
number two. (bell dings)

00:04:22.009 --> 00:04:25.253
- I can't say I'm too surprised
with the mac and cheeses

00:04:25.253 --> 00:04:26.086
people picked.

00:04:26.086 --> 00:04:27.965
While the show stopper took
the most time and effort,

00:04:27.965 --> 00:04:29.494
it amazed everyone that ate it.

00:04:29.494 --> 00:04:31.002
Plus, it's the most versatile.

00:04:31.002 --> 00:04:33.137
There are countless ways for
you to customize the flavors

00:04:33.137 --> 00:04:34.683
and textures to make it your own.

00:04:34.683 --> 00:04:35.517
That being said,

00:04:35.517 --> 00:04:37.728
some people really liked
the box mac and cheese.

00:04:37.728 --> 00:04:40.065
If you want something
quick, cheap and nostalgic,

00:04:40.065 --> 00:04:40.898
go for it.

00:04:40.898 --> 00:04:42.458
If you want the simplicity and efficiency

00:04:42.458 --> 00:04:43.597
of the box mac and cheese,

00:04:43.597 --> 00:04:45.640
but with more flavor and flexibility,

00:04:45.640 --> 00:04:47.088
the one pot is your version.

00:04:47.088 --> 00:04:48.389
At the end of the day,

00:04:48.389 --> 00:04:49.412
mac and cheese is great,

00:04:49.412 --> 00:04:51.644
and you really can't go
wrong with any recipe.

00:04:51.644 --> 00:04:53.331
And I've had it like 10 times this week,

00:04:53.331 --> 00:04:55.570
but I haven't eaten all day.

00:04:55.570 --> 00:04:57.358
And I'm hungry.

00:04:57.358 --> 00:04:59.941
(upbeat music)

